id: pm-memory-sdk-transaction-reader
title: Adopt public SDK transaction inspection and native hash preconditions
description: "Adopt public SDK transaction readers, host-bound item batches and locked expected revisions while retaining portable history, read-set and forward-retention proofs."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[9]: "gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1576","gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1597","gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1598","gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1620",sdk-adoption,"upstream:pm-cli#1576","upstream:pm-cli#1597","upstream:pm-cli#1598","upstream:pm-cli#1620"
created_at: "2026-10-27T06:21:15.119Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T17:27:10.170Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Replace owned SDK journal reads with public transaction inspection without weakening crash recovery, CAS, foreign preservation or replay tests"
parent: pm-memory-0kwy
comments[18]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T08:53:47.062Z",codex-agent,"Additional verified SDK adapter limit: previewItemMutations accepts only pmRoot, transactionId, author and mutations; no include/exclude path or authoritative-item projection option exists. Its owned snapshot includes extensions, so installed dependency links can refuse normal imports. The package now projects SDK-certified item documents, relevant exact history streams and guarded SDK schema/settings into a private disposable tracker before invoking the same SDK validator. PmClient still has no host-bound preview method (related upstream issue 1598); that issue covers the public host-context surface, while this managed-directory scoping constraint is a separate observed symptom. Adopt a public scoped preview when available; do not remove validation or copy installed code."
  "2026-10-27T09:39:43.693Z",codex-agent,"Capability precision: runWorkspaceTransactionGc(dryRun: true) provides status/age sweep decisions, but not the ownership payload or step results needed for recovery, abandonment or replanning. It is not a substitute for the missing full transaction receipt reader tracked by 1597. No GC of foreign or SDK journals was added."
  "2026-10-29T02:15:08.111Z",codex-agent,"Portable import review confirms the remaining native read-to-write gap: the installed public update options have no expectedItemHash precondition (upstream 1576), and commitWorkspaceTransaction serializes transactions without excluding ordinary SDK/CLI writes (upstream 1620, verified on SDK 2026.10.25 and 2026.10.28). Future adoption must replace best-effort final hash/history rereads with the public native precondition when available. Existing receipt-payload reader/abandon/replan and scoped staged-document preview needs remain tracked by upstream 1597/1598. Current compensation cancels creations, preserves incoming/outgoing references, checks the real SDK proposal for unowned field side effects, and restores only still-owned field values; it does not claim native-writer isolation. Evidence and reverts remain on pm-memory-1363 and PR 15."
  "2026-10-29T05:58:06.040Z",codex-agent,"Round 13 removes import rollback entirely. Imports retain completed forward writes; legacy intents are retired without replay or restoration. Final pre-write SDK-normalized base/history checks remain best effort against ordinary native writers (#1576/#1620). The pinned previewItemMutations declaration still accepts only Pick<CommitItemMutationsOptions, pmRoot | transactionId | author | mutations>; no scoped projection argument is available. No new upstream issue was filed. Removing links to deleted rollback/replan modules; current work and behavioral evidence remain on pm-memory-1363 and PR 15."
  "2026-10-29T06:00:03.706Z",codex-agent,"Upstream status refresh: #1576 and #1620 remain OPEN. #1597 and #1598 are CLOSED; receipt inspection and host-bound/scoped preview are pinned-2026.10.25 compatibility needs, not current open upstream defects. The supported host floor and repository pin are unchanged. Adoption in a future dependency update should verify the new public declarations before replacing compatibility adapters."
  "2026-11-02T04:42:45.845Z",pi-memory,"Thread PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6yXN3S (P3): the task description still presented the closed upstream #1597/#1598 as open and omitted the open native precondition blockers (#1576/#1620). Description updated to reflect the closed status and the open blockers so the task no longer reads as actionable today."
  "2026-11-02T04:42:49.648Z",pi-memory,"Thread PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6yXN3S (P3): the task description still presented the closed upstream #1597/#1598 as open and omitted the open native precondition blockers (#1576/#1620). Description updated to reflect the closed status and the open blockers so the task no longer reads as actionable today."
  "2026-11-02T06:42:47.157Z",codex-sol,"Continuation audit of cubic thread PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6yXN3S: verified upstream states live: #1597/#1598 CLOSED, #1576/#1620 OPEN. Removed the inherited contradictory phrase claiming no acceptance criterion was blocked; the existing acceptance criterion still requires a supported public replacement without weakening native preconditions. Compatibility status and open blockers are now explicit. No upstream mutation was made."
  "2026-11-02T08:27:48.899Z",codex-sol,"Local strict project health has a host-only optional-extension skew: the pinned package SDK is 2026.10.27 while the globally installed pm-github advertises 2026.11.2. The pinned no-extensions health check passes 10/10 with zero warnings. Pins and global installations were retained. Clean CI installation remains the full health gate; this does not establish an SDK protocol defect or satisfy the still-open native-precondition blockers."
  "2026-11-06T10:08:55.719Z",codex-sol,"Implements companion pm-cli-website-tdwu G1. Reuse the existing owner item; public readers replace private journal paths and shapes, with native revision refusals supplementing immutable history and field ownership checks. Full release gates are delegated to CI per task; targeted real-tracker regressions, lint and typecheck run locally."
  "2026-11-06T10:09:38.889Z",codex-sol,"SDK batch compensation restores values and its create inspection adopts an existing id; those semantics differ from portable forward-only retention and positive creation ownership. Keep the domain coordinator and final ownership hook for source publication; use host-bound batches for independent birth construction and host-bound preview for canonical staging, plus withExpectedItemRevisions around source updates. Public abandonment is restricted to exact owned custom steps and never applied to foreign or item-batch recovery plans."
  "2026-11-06T10:32:18.611Z",codex-sol,"Validation: focused portable/adoption suite passed 79/79 tests with concurrency 2. Linked transaction regressions passed 5/5 through pm test --run --progress. Disposable behavioral reverts: native revision scope 2 failures; public receipt reader 1; public occupied-identity reader 1; supported retirement 1. Restoring the implementation passed all 15 adoption regressions. Concurrent edits, ABA/history-prefix rewrite, create-if-absent/foreign births, interrupted replay and compensation controls remain covered. Typecheck, lint, duplication, docstrings and identity checks pass; full npm/Bun release gates are delegated to CI per task."
  "2026-11-06T11:39:32.487Z",codex-sol,"CI on the prior head passed 703/703 tests in both Node 26 runtime gates but failed unchanged coverage thresholds: portable-ownership.ts had the final no-usable-receipt return unexercised. Earlier malformed fixtures are rejected by the public reader before package receipt inspection. Extend the counterfeit-schema regression with genuine SDK-coordinated empty, foreign and unrelated-target result payloads, proving they grant no ownership and do not mutate tracker state."
  "2026-11-06T11:53:25.282Z",codex-sol,"Coverage correction verified with genuine SDK coordinators: empty, scalar, array, foreign-owner, invalid-target, unrelated-target, pending and missing receipts grant no body ownership and leave observed tracker state unchanged. The focused c8 probe now has no uncovered branches in committedReceipt (whole-module coverage remains a separate full-suite claim). Linked transaction regressions passed 5/5 through pm test --run --progress. Prior Node 26 npm/Bun CI each passed 703/703 assertions but failed the unchanged coverage gate; fresh final-head CI must certify the complete scope."
  "2026-11-06T14:44:49.645Z",codex-sol,"Review round 3 raises an outside-diff ownership boundary: author and step fields alone do not establish package ownership of a workspace transaction. Add a durable package marker through public recoveryData, prove matching-field foreign transactions remain untouched, and retain legacy unmarked receipts without acquiring their compensation authority. Companion pm-cli-website-tdwu remains read only."
  "2026-11-06T15:03:05.250Z",codex-sol,"Review round 3 fixed: new attempt and publication coordinators carry exact package recoveryData markers bound to transaction, author and step. Recovery validates the marker before publishing and again under the abandonment lock. Legacy unmarked receipts are retained without being published or abandoned, preserving their native forward writes. Same-author/same-step foreign, legacy, and missing-receipt controls use genuine SDK trackers. Targeted adoption/publication/recovery suite passes 54/54; final linked adoption file passes 21/21 and marker subset 5/5. Function-only reverts fail: retirement 2, recovery publication 1, attempt creation 1 and write creation 1; restoration passes all five controls. A focused coverage probe exercises all newly added ownership conditions; full-scope coverage remains for CI. Typecheck, lint, duplication 0 percent and docstrings pass. The separate pre-existing quoted-key privacy bug is tracked in pm-memory-quoted-credential-keys with gh:unbraind/pm-memory#52 and is not claimed fixed. Companion pm-cli-website-tdwu remains read only."
  "2026-11-06T16:45:48.342Z",codex-sol,CI on 8184847 passed all 710 tests but missed one branch in validFields at unchanged 100 percent thresholds. Added a malformed baseline-array control built from a genuine SDK export; it refuses at parsing and before native writes. Named array properties also prove the explicit array rejection rather than relying on missing keys. No runtime ownership logic changed.
  "2026-11-06T17:27:01.532Z",codex-sol,"The linked malformed baseline-array control passes 1/1 on the final local source. The wider SDK/admission assertions pass in the 62-case run; its only failure was a separate wall-time privacy control, which subsequently passes in the unchanged six-case deadline run. No G1 runtime implementation changed for the coverage repair. Full-source coverage remains for fresh CI."
